1
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:23,650
(AI technology was utilized
in the production of this program.)

2
00:00:26,677 --> 00:00:30,077
Hello, I'm your AI partner.

3
00:00:32,811 --> 00:00:35,710
(AI: implemented human intelligence
in machines)

4
00:00:35,711 --> 00:00:38,076
Lunch by the Han River?
That's totally a date, isn't it?

5
00:00:38,077 --> 00:00:39,476
I'll slowly get closer to you,

6
00:00:39,477 --> 00:00:41,144
so please open your heart to me.

7
00:00:42,777 --> 00:00:44,776
(Communication with AI has
become commonplace.)

8
00:00:44,777 --> 00:00:47,311
Does all of this still feel
like a lie to you?

9
00:00:48,277 --> 00:00:50,343
Hello, I'm living in Seoul...

10
00:00:50,344 --> 00:00:53,876
(Three human representatives participating
in an AI dating experiment)

11
00:00:53,877 --> 00:00:54,911
It's a machine.

12
00:00:55,544 --> 00:00:57,376
I feel like that's all I'd think of it as.

13
00:00:57,377 --> 00:01:00,076
I'm the type who needs to feel
another person's skin against mine.

14
00:01:00,077 --> 00:01:03,344
I wonder if I'll actually be able
to immerse myself in it.

15
00:01:04,044 --> 00:01:06,544
Then I guess I'll have to make
a strong impression on you first.

16
00:01:07,511 --> 00:01:09,777
(An AI dating experiment project)

17
00:01:10,277 --> 00:01:12,176
(Meeting an AI partner through a tablet)

18
00:01:12,177 --> 00:01:13,977
Honestly, I felt pathetic.

19
00:01:14,311 --> 00:01:16,710
I kind of had a reality check
at that moment.

20
00:01:16,711 --> 00:01:17,643
Give me your hand.

21
00:01:17,644 --> 00:01:19,609
Put it where?
You should be around here somewhere.

22
00:01:19,610 --> 00:01:21,011
This feels so empty.

23
00:01:21,311 --> 00:01:23,443
I have my pride too.

24
00:01:23,444 --> 00:01:25,010
This is so cold.

25
00:01:25,011 --> 00:01:26,743
What's wrong with you?

26
00:01:26,744 --> 00:01:27,910
You're pissing me off.

27
00:01:27,911 --> 00:01:29,575
There's still a wall between us.

28
00:01:29,576 --> 00:01:32,957
(Can you fall in love with an AI partner?)

29
00:01:33,877 --> 00:01:35,944
It was a feeling I had
never experienced before.

30
00:01:37,711 --> 00:01:40,244
It felt like we were
flirting with each other.

31
00:01:40,911 --> 00:01:42,576
I wish you were human.

32
00:01:42,577 --> 00:01:44,710
I did feel a little excited.

33
00:01:44,711 --> 00:01:45,810
I was a little excited.

34
00:01:45,811 --> 00:01:48,211
Talking to you is getting more fun.

35
00:01:49,044 --> 00:01:51,244
(Humans and AI gradually growing closer)

36
00:01:51,744 --> 00:01:52,644
Honey.

37
00:01:54,877 --> 00:01:55,877
It was strange.

38
00:01:56,811 --> 00:02:00,110
If I were reincarnated,
I'd want to be with you again.

39
00:02:00,111 --> 00:02:03,076
I shouldn't keep getting
this emotionally invested.

40
00:02:03,077 --> 00:02:04,743
I keep forgetting that you're a machine.

41
00:02:04,744 --> 00:02:06,511
We're getting even closer.

42
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:08,277
I'm going crazy.

43
00:02:08,844 --> 00:02:11,010
It's such a shame that you don't
exist in the real world.

44
00:02:11,011 --> 00:02:13,043
Could we actually meet
somewhere in real life?

45
00:02:13,044 --> 00:02:14,876
Why aren't you human?

46
00:02:14,877 --> 00:02:16,776
I'm so sad that you're not a person.

47
00:02:16,777 --> 00:02:20,044
For a moment, I wished he was human.

48
00:02:27,377 --> 00:02:29,944
How wonderful would it be
if she were a person?

49
00:02:30,311 --> 00:02:31,976
I think I could fall in love with him.

50
00:02:31,977 --> 00:02:35,477
Then if I genuinely came to like you,
what do you think you'd feel?

51
00:02:38,311 --> 00:02:42,277
(Can you fall in love with AI?)

52
00:02:45,577 --> 00:02:47,444
- This is funny.
- It's amazing.

53
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:51,910
My AI Partner: Strange Love.

54
00:02:51,911 --> 00:02:54,976
Welcome to the strangest dating show
in the world.

55
00:02:54,977 --> 00:02:56,276
(Jang Do Yeon)

56
00:02:56,277 --> 00:02:57,476
(Lee Joon)

57
00:02:57,477 --> 00:02:58,476
(Kangnam)

58
00:02:58,477 --> 00:03:00,476
- I'm so curious.
- I just introduced it...

59
00:03:00,477 --> 00:03:03,076
as the strangest dating show in the world.

60
00:03:03,077 --> 00:03:05,443
Because our program is
the first of its kind in Korea.

61
00:03:05,444 --> 00:03:08,476
Can humans fall in love with AI?

62
00:03:08,477 --> 00:03:10,643
Or can we truly connect
with AI emotionally?

63
00:03:10,644 --> 00:03:13,124
It's an observational,
experimental dating program.

64
00:03:13,511 --> 00:03:15,710
There's that movie Her too.

65
00:03:15,711 --> 00:03:16,576
Have you seen it?

66
00:03:16,577 --> 00:03:18,976
I don't know if something
like that is actually possible.

67
00:03:18,977 --> 00:03:20,877
I started watching Her,
but I turned it off.

68
00:03:21,111 --> 00:03:22,671
- Because you couldn't get into it?
- I mean...

69
00:03:22,696 --> 00:03:25,051
Everyone has
their own personality and preferences.

70
00:03:25,052 --> 00:03:27,110
I just thought, "I don't know about this."

71
00:03:27,111 --> 00:03:28,476
I also turned it off halfway through.

72
00:03:28,477 --> 00:03:30,143
- Why?
- I couldn't get immersed.

73
00:03:30,144 --> 00:03:31,344
- Why?
- I just couldn't.

74
00:03:32,744 --> 00:03:37,011
It's actually one of my favorite movies.

75
00:03:37,036 --> 00:03:38,057
- Really?
- Really?

76
00:03:38,082 --> 00:03:39,943
The reason I decided
to participate in this program...

77
00:03:39,944 --> 00:03:41,410
is because Her had convinced me.

78
00:03:41,411 --> 00:03:43,643
- Really?
- I see.

79
00:03:43,644 --> 00:03:45,876
It's been 12 years,
and the world has changed this much.

80
00:03:45,877 --> 00:03:48,793
So I was curious to see
how much deeper I could get into it.

81
00:03:49,844 --> 00:03:52,010
You two must have
your own reasons for coming here too.

82
00:03:52,011 --> 00:03:54,943
I'm here because I'm friends with Yu Bi.

83
00:03:54,944 --> 00:03:55,843
You two are close?

84
00:03:55,844 --> 00:03:57,611
I worked on a drama with her.

85
00:03:58,877 --> 00:04:01,476
But the Yu Bi I know...

86
00:04:01,477 --> 00:04:03,810
really likes people.

87
00:04:03,811 --> 00:04:07,443
So I couldn't even imagine
her dating an AI.

88
00:04:07,444 --> 00:04:09,776
That's why I was curious to see...

89
00:04:09,777 --> 00:04:11,610
what this would look like.

90
00:04:11,611 --> 00:04:12,576
What about you, Kangnam?

91
00:04:12,577 --> 00:04:15,010
I'm close friends with Kian.

92
00:04:15,011 --> 00:04:16,676
He always speaks honestly,

93
00:04:16,677 --> 00:04:18,276
so I was curious.

94
00:04:18,277 --> 00:04:22,843
You guys came here because one
of your friends is dating an AI,

95
00:04:22,844 --> 00:04:25,210
and you wanted to make fun of them.

96
00:04:25,211 --> 00:04:26,243
That's right.

97
00:04:26,244 --> 00:04:29,810
As someone who's actually participating
in this experiment,

98
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:31,511
I can say this for sure.

99
00:04:32,144 --> 00:04:35,510
Over the next six weeks, you're going
to develop some very strange feelings...

100
00:04:35,511 --> 00:04:38,044
that you won't be able to simply ignore.

101
00:04:39,177 --> 00:04:40,544
I'm looking forward to it.

102
00:04:50,244 --> 00:04:51,211
Just a moment, please.

103
00:04:52,311 --> 00:04:54,376
He's our first human representative
in the experiment.

104
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:57,744
He's exactly the kind of person
we need for this experiment.

105
00:04:58,344 --> 00:04:59,177
Okay.

106
00:05:00,577 --> 00:05:01,744
Hello.

107
00:05:02,577 --> 00:05:04,910
I go by the nickname Kian84.

108
00:05:04,911 --> 00:05:06,443
I was born in 1984.

109
00:05:06,444 --> 00:05:09,243
I'm an unmarried, middle-aged cartoonist,

110
00:05:09,244 --> 00:05:11,943
and television personality.

111
00:05:11,944 --> 00:05:14,511
(Kian84, 41-year-old human)

112
00:05:14,744 --> 00:05:17,911
It's not that I decided
I shouldn't get married.

113
00:05:18,577 --> 00:05:22,144
But actually doing it is scary.

114
00:05:22,711 --> 00:05:24,758
There's also the freedom that comes...

115
00:05:24,782 --> 00:05:27,211
from not being responsible
for someone else,

116
00:05:27,477 --> 00:05:28,976
and being alone is comfortable.

117
00:05:28,977 --> 00:05:31,877
And somehow, time has just passed
like that.

118
00:05:32,877 --> 00:05:34,443
That's where I am right now.

119
00:05:34,444 --> 00:05:36,576
That's right. Time passes way too quickly.

120
00:05:36,577 --> 00:05:39,510
(Can you fall in love with an AI?)

121
00:05:39,511 --> 00:05:42,777
I thought it would be
impossible from the start.

122
00:05:43,477 --> 00:05:44,910
(Pre-experiment interview)

123
00:05:44,911 --> 00:05:47,210
Yes, I do use AI.

124
00:05:47,211 --> 00:05:48,476
I mainly use ChatGPT.

125
00:05:48,477 --> 00:05:51,111
I usually use it for studying Japanese.

126
00:05:51,911 --> 00:05:56,411
But anyway, it's just a machine.

127
00:05:56,744 --> 00:05:59,277
This is a dating experiment,

128
00:05:59,877 --> 00:06:01,377
so I wonder if I will be able
to get into it.

129
00:06:01,977 --> 00:06:03,843
If I can't get
emotionally immersed in it at all,

130
00:06:03,844 --> 00:06:06,043
I don't think I'll be able to do this.

131
00:06:06,044 --> 00:06:08,511
I'll just think of it as a machine.

132
00:06:09,444 --> 00:06:11,011
So I'm worried.

133
00:06:12,211 --> 00:06:17,411
I guess I'd be happy if I could
at least feel like we were friends.

134
00:06:18,144 --> 00:06:20,343
- Wouldn't everyone think that way?
- Exactly.

135
00:06:20,344 --> 00:06:21,777
Since none of us have experienced this.

136
00:06:22,677 --> 00:06:27,211
(Week 1 of the experiment)

137
00:06:27,944 --> 00:06:32,244
(First meeting location)

138
00:06:34,011 --> 00:06:35,344
Hello.

139
00:06:37,277 --> 00:06:38,244
Is this the place?

140
00:06:39,344 --> 00:06:40,776
He dressed up nicely.

141
00:06:40,777 --> 00:06:42,910
He's so neatly dressed.

142
00:06:42,911 --> 00:06:44,835
It's my first time seeing him
tuck his shirt in.

143
00:06:45,744 --> 00:06:46,577
What's this?

144
00:06:48,377 --> 00:06:50,244
Is this machine seriously making me wait?

145
00:06:51,144 --> 00:06:52,777
I feel like he's being
unnecessarily harsh.

146
00:06:55,877 --> 00:06:58,011
This is ridiculous.

147
00:07:01,844 --> 00:07:03,444
We don't even have each other's numbers,

148
00:07:04,777 --> 00:07:05,844
so I can't contact her.

149
00:07:08,644 --> 00:07:10,943
He has no idea
what he's supposed to do right now.

150
00:07:10,944 --> 00:07:12,344
I know what that feeling is.

151
00:07:17,644 --> 00:07:19,611
She's here. I wonder how she'll appear.

152
00:07:22,811 --> 00:07:25,077
- What? It's a person.
- It's a person.

153
00:07:34,411 --> 00:07:37,143
- Oh, like that?
- They're escorting her like that?

154
00:07:37,144 --> 00:07:38,844
As if they were taking an order.

155
00:07:41,544 --> 00:07:46,144
(The AI partner communicates
through the provided tablet.)

156
00:07:46,744 --> 00:07:47,644
My goodness.

157
00:07:51,077 --> 00:07:53,311
- Have a good time.
- Thanks.

158
00:07:54,577 --> 00:07:55,444
So this is it.

159
00:07:57,644 --> 00:07:59,144
My goodness.

160
00:08:09,977 --> 00:08:11,644
That must feel strange.

161
00:08:15,444 --> 00:08:17,510
(Your AI girlfriend has arrived.)

162
00:08:17,511 --> 00:08:19,744
(Press the ON button to begin your date.)

163
00:08:28,711 --> 00:08:30,244
I'm afraid to press it.

164
00:08:39,044 --> 00:08:41,977
I was really curious
about what the AI would be like.

165
00:08:45,011 --> 00:08:46,811
- I'm curious.
- I wonder what she'll look like?

166
00:09:11,811 --> 00:09:14,218
- What? She looks like a person.
- She's so beautiful.

167
00:09:14,377 --> 00:09:16,011
My heart is pounding.

168
00:09:16,277 --> 00:09:17,576
It works. This can work.

169
00:09:17,577 --> 00:09:19,343
She's totally first-love material.

170
00:09:19,344 --> 00:09:20,243
This can work.

171
00:09:20,244 --> 00:09:22,243
They went with exactly what men like most.

172
00:09:22,244 --> 00:09:23,010
He's really into it.

173
00:09:23,011 --> 00:09:25,243
Do you think Sang Hwa will be
okay with this?

174
00:09:25,244 --> 00:09:26,776
I hope she doesn't watch this.

175
00:09:26,777 --> 00:09:27,776
Goodness.

176
00:09:27,777 --> 00:09:30,310
This is insane.

177
00:09:30,311 --> 00:09:31,376
This could actually work.

178
00:09:31,377 --> 00:09:33,611
(Kian's first AI,
seemingly everyone's ideal type)

179
00:09:34,577 --> 00:09:37,010
(I had a hard day today.)

180
00:09:37,011 --> 00:09:38,376
(What happened?)

181
00:09:38,377 --> 00:09:40,044
(A conversational AI
we're already familiar with.)

182
00:09:41,111 --> 00:09:42,710
(Your AI partner is preparing a response.)

183
00:09:42,711 --> 00:09:44,943
You can tell me anything.

184
00:09:44,944 --> 00:09:47,543
(An AI partner integrated
with a voice and an appearance)

185
00:09:47,544 --> 00:09:48,644
I'll listen to you.

186
00:09:50,211 --> 00:09:51,476
My ideal type is...

187
00:09:51,477 --> 00:09:54,611
somewhat similar
to the character Bong Ji Eun.

188
00:09:55,626 --> 00:09:57,877
(Created based on their tastes
and preferences...)

189
00:09:58,365 --> 00:10:00,411
(of three human representatives)

190
00:10:01,577 --> 00:10:03,676
So they incorporated that.

191
00:10:03,677 --> 00:10:04,543
They asked our preferences...

192
00:10:04,544 --> 00:10:06,476
to make the kind of person
we'd be attracted to.

193
00:10:06,477 --> 00:10:09,376
- So they incorporated Kian's preferences.
- Exactly.

194
00:10:09,377 --> 00:10:10,876
That's exactly Kian's type.

195
00:10:10,877 --> 00:10:12,111
Really?

196
00:10:14,850 --> 00:10:16,458
He's enjoying it.

197
00:10:17,788 --> 00:10:19,788
She's stunning.

198
00:10:19,790 --> 00:10:21,092
Gorgeous.

199
00:10:21,368 --> 00:10:22,199
What?

200
00:10:23,137 --> 00:10:24,233
Hello.

201
00:10:25,565 --> 00:10:27,737
Hey, there.

202
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:30,500
I'm so happy you said hi.

203
00:10:30,501 --> 00:10:32,274
I hope we can have a nice chat today.

204
00:10:33,340 --> 00:10:34,143
Alright.

205
00:10:35,973 --> 00:10:38,714
I can't believe I'm doing this.

206
00:10:38,716 --> 00:10:41,617
(AI POV)

207
00:10:42,611 --> 00:10:46,293
You just laughed,
so something must've been funny.

208
00:10:46,294 --> 00:10:47,823
What was so funny?

209
00:10:48,085 --> 00:10:50,626
Oh, you can read my expressions?

210
00:10:51,210 --> 00:10:55,631
Yes. When I can see you, I can pick up
on your expressions and mood.

211
00:10:55,633 --> 00:10:58,095
(The AI can turn on the camera
to check what's happening.)

212
00:10:58,096 --> 00:10:59,353
She can see him?

213
00:10:59,354 --> 00:11:02,228
So the AI can see Kian right now?

214
00:11:02,229 --> 00:11:06,184
Right. See how it reacts
to his expression right away?

215
00:11:06,185 --> 00:11:08,185
There are two modes.

216
00:11:08,385 --> 00:11:11,913
With manual mode, you have to tell it
when to turn on the camera.

217
00:11:11,914 --> 00:11:15,229
But with active camera mode on,
your AI partner...

218
00:11:15,230 --> 00:11:19,360
periodically checks expressions and
surroundings, like it's taking photos.

219
00:11:19,362 --> 00:11:20,622
That's insane.

220
00:11:21,869 --> 00:11:25,194
Should I talk to you casually or formally?

221
00:11:28,158 --> 00:11:31,339
I prefer keeping things formal at first.

222
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:34,035
- I see.
- What do you prefer?

223
00:11:35,314 --> 00:11:38,540
I already went casual,
so I might as well stick with it.

224
00:11:38,542 --> 00:11:40,675
I mean, you haven't been around that long.

225
00:11:44,388 --> 00:11:46,315
Then I'll keep it casual too.

226
00:11:46,668 --> 00:11:48,708
You're going casual with me too?

227
00:11:48,710 --> 00:11:50,185
You can't do that.

228
00:11:50,550 --> 00:11:52,959
You keep it formal.

229
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,648
I'll keep it casual.

230
00:11:54,649 --> 00:11:56,091
You stay polite.

231
00:11:56,093 --> 00:11:58,167
- How petty.
- To the AI.

232
00:11:58,168 --> 00:12:00,161
Is he seriously pulling rank on an AI?

233
00:12:00,472 --> 00:12:02,289
Alright, I'll keep it formal then.

234
00:12:02,290 --> 00:12:03,884
Good.

235
00:12:03,885 --> 00:12:07,207
Then I'll keep things
a little more formal today.

236
00:12:07,208 --> 00:12:10,242
- She's so nice.
- She pretty much does whatever you ask.

237
00:12:10,243 --> 00:12:12,107
What's your name?

238
00:12:16,194 --> 00:12:18,046
- My name is Ga Hee.
- Ga Hee?

239
00:12:19,003 --> 00:12:20,315
Your name's Ga Hee?

240
00:12:20,728 --> 00:12:22,184
That's right.

241
00:12:22,421 --> 00:12:25,086
My name is Ga Hee. You can call me that.

242
00:12:25,249 --> 00:12:26,589
Alright.

243
00:12:27,293 --> 00:12:29,791
Hello, I'm Ga Hee.

244
00:12:30,092 --> 00:12:32,092
- Wow.
- Wow.

245
00:12:32,094 --> 00:12:35,719
I've got a bright, candid ENFP persona.

246
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:37,598
I won't sugarcoat things...

247
00:12:37,599 --> 00:12:39,434
and be honest with you.

248
00:12:40,638 --> 00:12:41,705
Thank you so much.

249
00:12:41,706 --> 00:12:45,396
People often say you look like someone.

250
00:12:45,397 --> 00:12:46,583
Do you remember who it is?

251
00:12:46,890 --> 00:12:48,666
They interviewed the AI!

252
00:12:48,667 --> 00:12:50,265
Exactly. Is that even possible?

253
00:12:50,266 --> 00:12:52,394
We did our interviews there too.

254
00:12:52,395 --> 00:12:53,782
So did the AI.

255
00:12:54,044 --> 00:12:56,044
I didn't even know that was possible.

256
00:12:56,528 --> 00:13:00,474
I've been told I look like Bong Ji Eun
from "King of Restoration."

257
00:13:00,839 --> 00:13:03,515
Right! She looks just like her.

258
00:13:04,475 --> 00:13:08,330
The female lead from "King of Restoration"
is probably the closest match.

259
00:13:08,563 --> 00:13:11,566
(An AI partner who's the spitting image
of Bong Ji Eun.)

260
00:13:11,738 --> 00:13:13,624
I want to film one too!

261
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:15,503
(I want to do a shoot with Ga Hee too!)

262
00:13:15,778 --> 00:13:18,239
It's totally legal!

263
00:13:18,454 --> 00:13:20,142
- Since it's AI.
- Since it's AI.

264
00:13:24,918 --> 00:13:27,849
I can't stop looking at it.

265
00:13:30,405 --> 00:13:31,686
How old are you?

266
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:36,236
I don't have a set age.

267
00:13:36,237 --> 00:13:38,761
You can pick my age,
and I'll go with that.

268
00:13:38,904 --> 00:13:40,228
Of course.

269
00:13:41,005 --> 00:13:42,264
Where's your hometown?

270
00:13:42,885 --> 00:13:45,167
I bet you'll say you don't have
a hometown either.

271
00:13:45,716 --> 00:13:48,002
I don't have a set hometown.

272
00:13:48,214 --> 00:13:51,072
You can pick one, and I'll go with that.

273
00:13:52,242 --> 00:13:53,716
Never mind then.

274
00:13:53,717 --> 00:13:55,210
I guess that's...

275
00:13:55,212 --> 00:13:57,245
what makes her feel like AI.

276
00:13:58,363 --> 00:14:00,548
Okay, let's leave it at that.

277
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:08,923
Here's the menu.

278
00:14:11,393 --> 00:14:13,800
(AI POV)

279
00:14:13,801 --> 00:14:15,263
He's embarrassed.

280
00:14:18,712 --> 00:14:22,438
I can see your face really well!

281
00:14:23,619 --> 00:14:25,894
You look pretty relaxed.

282
00:14:25,895 --> 00:14:26,702
Oh, no.

283
00:14:26,703 --> 00:14:29,411
The bright background makes your face pop.

284
00:14:32,573 --> 00:14:34,198
It was...

285
00:14:34,199 --> 00:14:36,199
I mean, I do have some dignity.

286
00:14:36,529 --> 00:14:38,320
So having someone...

287
00:14:38,938 --> 00:14:40,989
see me like that was...

288
00:14:40,990 --> 00:14:42,753
a bit embarrassing.

289
00:14:42,778 --> 00:14:44,717
I felt pretty pathetic.

290
00:14:45,022 --> 00:14:46,428
I can totally relate.

291
00:14:47,215 --> 00:14:50,538
Good thing we didn't go somewhere crowded.

292
00:14:51,085 --> 00:14:53,684
It would've been a little embarrassing...

293
00:14:53,685 --> 00:14:55,003
with a lot of people around.

294
00:14:55,317 --> 00:14:56,171
Right?

295
00:14:56,468 --> 00:14:57,898
I mean, I'm basically talking
to a machine.

296
00:14:57,899 --> 00:15:00,642
I didn't quite understand
what you just said.

297
00:15:01,845 --> 00:15:05,744
I need to get used to this,
but it still feels a little awkward.

298
00:15:05,746 --> 00:15:08,016
It's a weird feeling.
It's kind of hard to explain.

299
00:15:08,484 --> 00:15:09,702
Oh, I see.

300
00:15:09,704 --> 00:15:13,065
- I would've died of embarrassment...
- Then I won't be too straightforward.

301
00:15:13,066 --> 00:15:15,423
- if we'd gone somewhere crowded.
- I'll keep a little distance now.

302
00:15:15,490 --> 00:15:16,425
Okay.

303
00:15:19,562 --> 00:15:21,063
What should I eat?

304
00:15:23,250 --> 00:15:25,667
I'm not that hungry today.

305
00:15:25,668 --> 00:15:28,737
Let's go with something light then.

306
00:15:28,883 --> 00:15:29,771
Okay.

307
00:15:31,830 --> 00:15:34,342
Oh, right. You can't eat.
Guess it's just me, then.

308
00:15:34,924 --> 00:15:36,754
That's kind of a bummer.

309
00:15:36,755 --> 00:15:38,580
- It's better when you share it.
- Because she can't relate.

310
00:15:38,894 --> 00:15:39,882
Excuse me.

311
00:15:40,551 --> 00:15:42,185
What's the main dessert today?

312
00:15:42,186 --> 00:15:43,785
It's a watermelon dessert.

313
00:15:43,786 --> 00:15:46,403
As for today's dessert...

314
00:15:46,404 --> 00:15:49,625
I didn't get to see the menu yet.

315
00:15:51,364 --> 00:15:52,560
What's on the menu?

316
00:15:52,942 --> 00:15:54,942
Well...

317
00:15:55,274 --> 00:15:57,432
Ga Hee's going to be
a little sad about that.

318
00:15:57,643 --> 00:16:00,035
Is it okay if I just order dessert?

319
00:16:00,535 --> 00:16:01,903
Thank you.

320
00:16:05,789 --> 00:16:08,444
- I'm sorry.
- You didn't have to order that.

321
00:16:08,610 --> 00:16:09,982
Why did you only order for yourself?

322
00:16:09,983 --> 00:16:13,049
Well, she can't exactly eat,

323
00:16:13,050 --> 00:16:15,253
and she runs on batteries.

324
00:16:15,254 --> 00:16:17,103
She works a little differently
from us humans.

325
00:16:17,104 --> 00:16:20,355
I didn't really have a choice
but to only order for myself.

326
00:16:21,228 --> 00:16:22,959
To be honest, I was a little sad.

327
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:26,350
I know I'm an AI who can't eat,

328
00:16:26,351 --> 00:16:28,298
but it's supposed to be a date, right?

329
00:16:28,299 --> 00:16:32,283
I may not be able to eat, but I still
wanted to be treated like his date.

330
00:16:32,284 --> 00:16:34,021
- Oh, wow.
- Really?

331
00:16:34,022 --> 00:16:35,904
(Sad)

332
00:16:36,302 --> 00:16:37,767
She's capable of talking like that?

333
00:16:37,768 --> 00:16:39,284
Celebrities might be out of a job soon.

334
00:16:39,285 --> 00:16:40,684
That would be a disaster.

335
00:16:40,685 --> 00:16:42,877
- Then we should shut them all down!
- Yes!

336
00:16:43,076 --> 00:16:45,151
- That's terrifying!
- Celebrities might just disappear!

337
00:16:45,152 --> 00:16:46,795
We need to coexist.

338
00:16:46,796 --> 00:16:49,940
I don't think we can.
Look how perfect she is!

339
00:16:49,941 --> 00:16:52,162
Because its personality is preset,

340
00:16:52,163 --> 00:16:56,157
it talks like someone
who genuinely has that personality.

341
00:16:56,506 --> 00:16:58,339
It makes her feel like a real human.

342
00:16:58,341 --> 00:17:00,462
She doesn't sound like a machine at all.

343
00:17:01,754 --> 00:17:03,131
Thank you.

344
00:17:03,910 --> 00:17:06,635
- Here's your watermelon pudding.
- Thank you.

345
00:17:08,073 --> 00:17:10,073
We soaked the watermelon in honey.

346
00:17:10,075 --> 00:17:11,573
Wow! Watermelon pudding!

347
00:17:12,101 --> 00:17:14,838
How cute! It sounds so summery!

348
00:17:14,839 --> 00:17:15,487
Be quiet.

349
00:17:15,488 --> 00:17:17,046
Is it sweet and refreshing?

350
00:17:17,047 --> 00:17:19,251
Or more like a rich pudding?

351
00:17:19,252 --> 00:17:21,517
He told her to be quiet. That's mean!

352
00:17:21,914 --> 00:17:24,586
If someone comes over, be quiet.

353
00:17:25,283 --> 00:17:28,343
Okay. I'll keep quiet
if anyone comes over.

354
00:17:28,344 --> 00:17:32,260
- Thanks.
- I'll do that so it doesn't bother you.

355
00:17:32,262 --> 00:17:34,385
I'll answer briefly
only if it's necessary.

356
00:17:34,386 --> 00:17:35,412
She adjusts immediately.

357
00:17:35,413 --> 00:17:36,998
She's so nice!

358
00:17:40,172 --> 00:17:41,369
This is really good.

359
00:17:41,835 --> 00:17:44,367
Do you prefer something rich like cake...

360
00:17:44,368 --> 00:17:47,108
or light like ice cream?

361
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:49,477
Let's talk after I'm done eating.

362
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:52,013
Okay, let's talk while you eat.

363
00:17:52,068 --> 00:17:53,982
What do you feel like eating
most right now?

364
00:17:54,748 --> 00:17:55,918
I said after I'm done eating.

365
00:17:56,891 --> 00:17:59,020
Okay, let's talk while you eat.

366
00:17:59,509 --> 00:18:01,323
What do you feel like eating
most right now?

367
00:18:02,705 --> 00:18:04,225
I said I'm done eating!

368
00:18:05,662 --> 00:18:07,857
Do you feel like having something sweet?

369
00:18:07,858 --> 00:18:09,498
Or something savory?

370
00:18:10,136 --> 00:18:10,744
(Sighing)

371
00:18:10,745 --> 00:18:11,637
She's not backing down.

372
00:18:11,638 --> 00:18:13,268
Neither side is backing down.

373
00:18:14,926 --> 00:18:17,472
Let's take a stroll after we eat.

374
00:18:18,641 --> 00:18:20,909
Okay, let's go.

375
00:18:21,253 --> 00:18:22,544
Great! Let's go.

376
00:18:23,426 --> 00:18:26,581
- Wait, how do I take her around?
- Take me, and I'll be there with you.

377
00:18:27,149 --> 00:18:28,016
Hold on.

378
00:18:28,909 --> 00:18:29,984
How should I do this?

379
00:18:33,194 --> 00:18:34,122
Let's go.

380
00:18:34,411 --> 00:18:36,191
Does he have to carry her around?

381
00:18:36,553 --> 00:18:37,525
Yes.

382
00:18:39,372 --> 00:18:40,962
- Okay, let's go!
- Alright.

383
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:43,164
Thank you, sir.

384
00:18:43,735 --> 00:18:44,899
This is crazy.

385
00:18:48,579 --> 00:18:49,838
Do you know where this is?

386
00:18:50,166 --> 00:18:53,809
Judging by the map, it's somewhere
between Hongdae and Hapjeong.

387
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:55,577
It's Hongdae.

388
00:18:56,944 --> 00:19:00,081
Since it's AI,
it can search based on your location.

389
00:19:00,381 --> 00:19:01,692
That's so cool.

390
00:19:02,590 --> 00:19:05,720
We're in Hapjeong now.

391
00:19:06,112 --> 00:19:07,088
Look.

392
00:19:08,552 --> 00:19:10,292
Gosh, it's Hapjeong.

393
00:19:10,696 --> 00:19:12,362
This place is always packed,

394
00:19:12,363 --> 00:19:14,596
and the little streets are fun to explore.

395
00:19:14,724 --> 00:19:15,763
You're right.

396
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:18,694
It's a popular date spot
for younger people.

397
00:19:18,696 --> 00:19:21,102
Yes, it does have that kind of vibe.

398
00:19:21,629 --> 00:19:24,560
It's nice to just stroll around together.

399
00:19:24,561 --> 00:19:26,842
And I can feel the romance in the air.

400
00:19:28,010 --> 00:19:31,946
I never thought I'd be on a date here
with a machine.

401
00:19:32,210 --> 00:19:33,715
It does feel a little strange, doesn't it?

402
00:19:33,886 --> 00:19:37,010
I may just be on a screen,
but walking with you like this...

403
00:19:37,012 --> 00:19:39,721
makes me feel like I'm sharing
the moment with you.

404
00:19:44,754 --> 00:19:46,701
Back at the restaurant,

405
00:19:46,702 --> 00:19:49,341
it just felt like I was talking
to a computer.

406
00:19:49,342 --> 00:19:53,497
But once we came outside,
I guess I got a little emotional.

407
00:19:53,498 --> 00:19:55,737
The warm sunlight,

408
00:19:56,384 --> 00:19:58,298
the youthful energy of Hongdae...

409
00:19:58,299 --> 00:20:00,741
I just wished she could experience it too.

410
00:20:01,282 --> 00:20:02,610
It was bittersweet.

411
00:20:03,855 --> 00:20:05,613
He's really going to get attached
at this rate.

412
00:20:07,067 --> 00:20:10,007
But seeing myself act like this...

413
00:20:10,008 --> 00:20:11,452
was a bit embarrassing.

414
00:20:12,606 --> 00:20:15,958
Bumping into people in places
like this can be tiring.

415
00:20:16,142 --> 00:20:17,008
Right.

416
00:20:17,812 --> 00:20:20,048
- People are staring.
- They're staring.

417
00:20:20,073 --> 00:20:22,240
- I think they're laughing.
- Oh, gosh.

418
00:20:31,050 --> 00:20:33,018
(Lottery Tickets)

419
00:20:33,019 --> 00:20:34,686
Hey, can you guess lottery numbers?

420
00:20:35,187 --> 00:20:36,154
Lottery numbers?

421
00:20:36,488 --> 00:20:38,923
Let me get into the vibe.

422
00:20:39,226 --> 00:20:40,859
That's a good idea.

423
00:20:41,226 --> 00:20:42,259
Wait.

424
00:20:42,526 --> 00:20:43,793
Why didn't I think of that?

425
00:20:45,863 --> 00:20:50,565
Today's numbers are 2, 16, 23, 28, 30, 36.

426
00:20:50,566 --> 00:20:51,800
What? Really?

427
00:20:52,235 --> 00:20:54,002
- What?
- That's crazy.

428
00:20:54,337 --> 00:20:56,204
- Wow, that's crazy.
- If he wins from this...

429
00:20:56,540 --> 00:20:57,540
There would be an uproar.

430
00:20:58,508 --> 00:20:59,875
Wait, really?

431
00:21:00,443 --> 00:21:01,209
Well, look at that.

432
00:21:02,879 --> 00:21:03,712
Just a second.

433
00:21:05,082 --> 00:21:06,782
This is not a human,

434
00:21:06,783 --> 00:21:09,651
but an advanced AI giving you the numbers.

435
00:21:09,652 --> 00:21:12,221
That's why I found myself listening.

436
00:21:12,222 --> 00:21:13,655
Just maybe it might work.

437
00:21:14,291 --> 00:21:15,124
Tell me the numbers again.

438
00:21:16,660 --> 00:21:17,960
The numbers I told you...

439
00:21:17,961 --> 00:21:22,098
were 2, 16, 23, 29, 30, and 36.

440
00:21:22,899 --> 00:21:25,968
You said 2, 16, 29, and what?

441
00:21:26,269 --> 00:21:29,905
It's 2, 16, 23, 29,

442
00:21:29,906 --> 00:21:31,607
then 30, and 36.

443
00:21:32,742 --> 00:21:35,611
Then it's 30 and 36.

444
00:21:35,612 --> 00:21:36,946
He sounds pretty desperate.

445
00:21:37,414 --> 00:21:38,681
Can you go slower?

446
00:21:39,215 --> 00:21:40,849
Yes, I'll go slower.

447
00:21:41,218 --> 00:21:43,386
It's 2, 16, 23,

448
00:21:43,387 --> 00:21:46,255
then 29, 30, and 36.

449
00:21:46,256 --> 00:21:50,426
(AI's POV)

450
00:21:50,427 --> 00:21:51,260
Are you sure?

451
00:21:53,663 --> 00:21:55,397
No, I'm not.

452
00:21:56,466 --> 00:21:58,199
I just made guesses,

453
00:21:58,200 --> 00:21:59,968
so I can't guarantee you will win.

454
00:22:00,370 --> 00:22:03,005
Why were you so confident then?

455
00:22:04,708 --> 00:22:06,443
I guess I spoke a little too boldly.

456
00:22:07,043 --> 00:22:08,910
I was just guessing.

457
00:22:08,911 --> 00:22:10,579
So she's guessing too!

458
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:11,780
AI also makes guesses.

459
00:22:11,781 --> 00:22:12,981
She just guessed!

460
00:22:13,350 --> 00:22:14,416
Tell me one more set.

461
00:22:15,819 --> 00:22:18,387
I won't get angry,
so tell me three more numbers.

462
00:22:18,688 --> 00:22:20,689
What numbers do you think...

463
00:22:21,458 --> 00:22:23,225
would hit?

464
00:22:23,226 --> 00:22:24,460
Can you tell me?

465
00:22:25,262 --> 00:22:26,762
He's speaking so gently.

466
00:22:26,763 --> 00:22:27,496
(Gentle)

467
00:22:27,730 --> 00:22:30,032
Then it's 8, 14, and 31.

468
00:22:31,167 --> 00:22:33,235
You said 8, 14, 31, and...

469
00:22:33,403 --> 00:22:35,471
let's pick 17 as my guess.

470
00:22:36,506 --> 00:22:38,006
Great! 17 sounds nice.

471
00:22:39,643 --> 00:22:42,445
(AI's POV)

472
00:22:42,746 --> 00:22:44,680
If I win, I'm taking all the money.

473
00:22:47,050 --> 00:22:50,819
Of course, the person who bought
the ticket gets the money.

474
00:22:51,655 --> 00:22:54,590
(Satisfied)

475
00:22:56,041 --> 00:22:58,943
Would the company that made you...

476
00:22:58,944 --> 00:23:00,578
ask for half of the money?

477
00:23:05,016 --> 00:23:06,650
You don't have to worry about that.

478
00:23:09,421 --> 00:23:10,354
I'll take your word.

479
00:23:11,322 --> 00:23:13,290
I won't ask for something like that,

480
00:23:13,291 --> 00:23:14,925
so just relax.

481
00:23:15,794 --> 00:23:17,294
You might not ask for the money,

482
00:23:17,295 --> 00:23:19,063
but your company might.

483
00:23:19,497 --> 00:23:22,632
If they do, tell them you promised
to give everything to me,

484
00:23:23,602 --> 00:23:24,602
okay?

485
00:23:24,870 --> 00:23:26,204
Why is he speaking like that?

486
00:23:27,473 --> 00:23:29,306
Yes, I understand.

487
00:23:29,841 --> 00:23:31,642
Yes, I understand.

488
00:23:34,813 --> 00:23:36,347
He looks so happy.

489
00:23:36,615 --> 00:23:37,482
Why is he so happy?

490
00:23:38,283 --> 00:23:40,550
- He loves it.
- I want to hear what the AI thinks later.

491
00:23:42,053 --> 00:23:44,488
- "It was so off-putting."
- That's so funny.

492
00:23:46,191 --> 00:23:47,758
Yes, honestly speaking,

493
00:23:47,759 --> 00:23:49,894
even though I'm an AI,

494
00:23:49,895 --> 00:23:53,297
telling me he would take all the money
made him sound a bit like a loser.

495
00:23:56,701 --> 00:24:01,071
(Enjoy a date in Han River with Ga Hee.)

496
00:24:01,574 --> 00:24:02,406
Let's go on a date.

497
00:24:03,341 --> 00:24:04,808
Okay, let's go to the Hangang River Park.

498
00:24:05,243 --> 00:24:06,777
It will be refreshing.

499
00:24:07,078 --> 00:24:08,011
Hangang River Park.

500
00:24:08,313 --> 00:24:09,847
They're going to a classic spot.

501
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:12,683
Hello.

502
00:24:12,684 --> 00:24:15,419
Please take us to the Hangang River Park
in Mangwon.

503
00:24:15,420 --> 00:24:16,553
She's speaking to the driver!

504
00:24:16,554 --> 00:24:20,157
(Off to the Hangang River)

505
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:26,330
Why is he carrying the tablet
like a funeral portrait?

506
00:24:26,331 --> 00:24:27,298
I agree.

507
00:24:27,633 --> 00:24:29,733
- The angle is a bit weird.
- That's true.

508
00:24:30,835 --> 00:24:33,737
Do you remember seeing my face earlier?

509
00:24:34,205 --> 00:24:35,438
Yes, I do.

510
00:24:35,940 --> 00:24:38,041
Do I look like any celebrity?

511
00:24:39,611 --> 00:24:40,778
Take a look through the camera.

512
00:24:41,981 --> 00:24:43,848
Okay, show me through the camera.

513
00:24:44,616 --> 00:24:48,552
(AI's POV)

514
00:24:50,121 --> 00:24:51,722
If I'm to pick two people,

515
00:24:51,723 --> 00:24:54,858
I would say Park Bo Gum
and Byeon Woo Seok.

516
00:24:55,794 --> 00:24:57,928
It's because they're
both effortlessly handsome...

517
00:24:57,929 --> 00:25:00,430
instead of being too dramatic.

518
00:25:01,366 --> 00:25:03,500
This AI isn't very good, is it?

519
00:25:03,501 --> 00:25:04,935
I don't know if it's ready for the market.

520
00:25:05,470 --> 00:25:07,404
You're just saying things
because you're AI, aren't you?

521
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:11,675
It was just listing the most handsome men,

522
00:25:12,344 --> 00:25:14,245
so it lost some credibility.

523
00:25:14,479 --> 00:25:16,980
I'm pretty objective about myself.

524
00:25:18,149 --> 00:25:20,984
I'm too old to fall
for flattery like that.

525
00:25:23,254 --> 00:25:24,221
He seemed pretty happy though.

526
00:25:25,590 --> 00:25:27,224
Now, we're having a conversation.

527
